{"reference":"Proverbs 26","book":"Proverbs","chapter":26,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Paired Sayings","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 4–5 place two apparently opposite instructions together: do not answer a fool according to his folly, yet answer a fool according to his folly. Proverbs often teaches through brief, context-sensitive generalizations set beside one another, rather than through rules that apply without exception. The pairing invites discernment: a response should not imitate foolishness, but silence may sometimes leave it appearing wise.","verse_refs":["Proverbs 26:4-5"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_proverbs_026_5440703198275712a77b109a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}